WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Diagnose first: root causes and action plans.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.170
Arga sells iced coffee from a cart near campus. Sales are down, and he already has a cure: a discount.

3
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:15.650
His friend asks one question first. What is the diagnosis? A cure for the wrong cause is not a cure.

4
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:24.300
He starts with a feeling: people think my coffee is too expensive. A feeling cannot be tested. So he writes a hypothesis with a number in it.

5
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:33.450
Before changing anything, he counts for one week. Twelve hundred people walk past the cart. Only three hundred notice it. One hundred and eighty buy, and one hundred and twenty of them come back.

6
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:39.710
His guess was wrong. Two in three buyers return.

7
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:45.520
The leak is earlier: most people never notice the cart.

8
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:53.880
Now he lists ideas, and sorts them by impact and ease. A tall sign and a brighter canopy: high impact, easy. First. Moving to the main gate would help more, but it is hard.

9
00:00:54.280 --> 00:01:02.240
Then every action gets an owner and a date. The sign, by Saturday. The canopy, by Monday. And in two weeks he counts again. A plan without owners and dates is only a wish.

10
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:09.640
Symptom, diagnosis, prescription. In that order. Write your guess with a number, so data can kill it.

11
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.440
Now it is your turn. Pick one problem you are about to fix. Write your hypothesis with a number before you act.
